Relevant tables & columns for the question  
olist_orders  
• order_id : identifier to be counted (number of delivered orders)  
• order_status : filter → only rows with value = 'delivered'  
• order_purchase_timestamp : extract year (2016‑2018) and month to aggregate the volumes  

Key filter / extraction conditions  
• WHERE order_status = 'delivered'  
• WHERE substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')  
• Year  = substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4)  
• Month = substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,7)   -- “YYYY‑MM”

Below are ten exploratory → final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively lead to the answer.

```sql
-- 1. See all different order_status values.
SELECT DISTINCT order_status
FROM olist_orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List the years present in the purchase timestamp (all statuses).
SELECT DISTINCT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year
FROM olist_orders
WHERE substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Total orders per year regardless of status (2016‑2018).
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year,
       COUNT(*) AS total_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Delivered orders per year (2016‑2018).
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year,
       COUNT(*)                         AS delivered_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
  AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Delivered orders per year, ascending by volume to spot the lowest year.
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year,
       COUNT(*) AS delivered_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
  AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY delivered_orders ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Delivered orders broken down by year‑month (all three years).
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,7) AS year_month,
       COUNT(*)                            AS delivered_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
  AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY year_month
ORDER BY year_month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Same as #6 but ordered by descending volume to see the biggest months overall.
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,7) AS year_month,
       COUNT(*)                            AS delivered_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
  AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY year_month
ORDER BY delivered_orders DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Identify which year has the lowest annual delivered orders (single row).
WITH year_totals AS (
  SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year,
         COUNT(*) AS delivered_orders
  FROM olist_orders
  WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
    AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
  GROUP BY year
)
SELECT year, delivered_orders
FROM year_totals
ORDER BY delivered_orders ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 9. Monthly delivered‑order volumes inside the year that was lowest in #8.
--    (Replace 2016 with the actual year returned by #8 if different.)
SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,7) AS year_month,
       COUNT(*)                            AS delivered_orders
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
  AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) = '2016'
GROUP BY year_month
ORDER BY delivered_orders DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Highest monthly delivered‑orders count in the lowest‑volume year.
--     (Again, replace 2016 with the correct year if #8 shows otherwise.)
WITH year_totals AS (
  SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) AS year,
         COUNT(*) AS delivered_orders
  FROM olist_orders
  WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
    AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
  GROUP BY year
),
lowest_year AS (
  SELECT year
  FROM year_totals
  ORDER BY delivered_orders ASC
  LIMIT 1
),
month_totals AS (
  SELECT substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,7) AS year_month,
         COUNT(*)                            AS delivered_orders
  FROM olist_orders, lowest_year
  WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
    AND substr(order_purchase_timestamp,1,4) = lowest_year.year
  GROUP BY year_month
)
SELECT MAX(delivered_orders) AS highest_monthly_volume_in_lowest_year
FROM month_totals;
```

